    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #339\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully to branch `bb/relay-134-heartbeat-agent-tools-01-04-pin-and-co-thr_ecr4dphfgd`.\n\n## Summary\n\nCloses #134: pins and contract-tests the pi runtime.\n\n- Added `@earendil-works/pi-ai`, `@earendil-works/pi-agent-core`, `@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent` (the real npm-published pi packages) to `@semprec/agent-runtime` at exact pinned version `0.85.1` — no range prefixes — with the lockfile updated so routine installs can't silently drift the version.\n- Added a named contract suite (`packages/agent-runtime/src/__tests__/piRuntimeContract.unit.test.ts`) exercising the real installed packages (no mocking of pi) to prove: tool execution defaults to parallel, constructing `Agent`/`AgentSession` never spawns a subprocess, `estimateContextTokens`/`shouldCompact` work on a bare message array without a running session, and the low-level `compact()` requires a prepared compaction rather than a bare array — checked both at runtime and at compile time via a `@ts-expect-error` assertion enforced by `tsc`. Also covers `resourceLoader.systemPromptOverride`.\n- Added a source-import lint (`check-pi-import-paths.mjs`) that fails if code reaches past the three documented package roots into internal/example pi paths.\n- Wired `pnpm run test:unit` and the new import-path lint into CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`), which previously ran no backend test tier at all.\n\nVerified in full: backend build, unit tests (90/90), integration tests (454/455 — the one failure is a pre-existing flaky race test in an unrelated file, reproducible on its own), e2e tests (5/5), migration-numbering check, module-boundary check, pi import-path lint, and the full web build/test suite (81/81) all pass.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
